48 Adam writes;466 values/17 leaves;all1024 inverse samples and both Jacobians/roundtrips/normalization/restore/immutability pass. Test NLL 2.878228426.
// result_end


> Check every forbidden conditioner derivative on actual stage inputs

The complete program re-evaluates each conditioner on a differentiable copy of
its actual stage input. For each of four blocks, four heads and128 test rows,
it records both input-coordinate partials:4,096 entries. Own/future inputs
account for 3,072 entries, all exactly zero. The remaining1,024 may be nonzero.
These are conditioner derivatives, distinct from the whole flow's input Jacobian;
stacking alternating blocks can give a dense whole-map Jacobian.

The left panel retains every forbidden partial; the right retains every allowed
partial. Flattening follows block, head, input coordinate, then original test-row
order, so each horizontal index refers to one recorded derivative entry.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/maf_strict_jacobians.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> out;for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/maf_density/outputs.npz"))out[k]=x;
 std::vector<n::Tensor> forbidden,allowed;
 for(int block=0;block<4;++block){auto degrees=n::models::MafMasks(block).input_degrees.to_vector<int>();
  for(int head=0;head<4;++head)for(int c=0;c<2;++c){auto value=n::select(out.at("conditioner_jacobian"+std::to_string(block)+"_"+std::to_string(head)),1,c);
   (degrees[c]>=degrees[head%2]?forbidden:allowed).push_back(value);}}
 auto zero=n::concat(forbidden,0),live=n::concat(allowed,0);
 if(zero.numel()!=3072||live.numel()!=1024||n::max(n::abs(zero)).item()!=0)throw std::runtime_error("Strict conditioner partials");
 auto panel=[&](const n::Tensor& y,const char* title){auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points(n::arange(0,y.numel()).to_vector<double>(),y.to_vector<double>(),"Every recorded entry",{37,99,235},2)
  .margins(78,22,54,70).y_limits(-.4,.4).x_label("Flattened derivative entry index").y_label("d(head) / d(stage input)").title(title);return p;};
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(panel(zero,"Forbidden: all 3072 exactly zero"))
 .add(panel(live,"Allowed: all 1024 retained")).size(1100,500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/maf_strict_jacobians.svg");
 n::save_npz("build/maf_strict_values.npz",{{"forbidden",zero},{"allowed",live}});
 std::print("All3072 forbidden conditioner partials are exactly zero;1024 allowed partials retained; max allowed absolute value {:.9f}.\n",n::max(n::abs(live)).item());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
All3072 forbidden conditioner partials are exactly zero;1024 allowed partials retained; max allowed absolute value 0.184919909.
\image(figures/maf_strict_jacobians.svg)
// result_end


\caption(All 4,096 actual conditioner derivatives are displayed. The 3,072 forbidden entries are exactly zero; allowed entries vary with stage input. The shared vertical scale distinguishes structural zeros from numerically small learned effects.)
\alttext(The left panel shows3072 blue zero partials along the horizontal axis. The right shows1024 allowed partials around zero, with visible nonzero values.)


> Inspect every observation without cutting off the high banana tail

The displayed pool scatter retains all 768 rows. Both coordinate axes span
[-4,7] at equal screen units, showing the test tail above y=5 that the source's
[-4,4] plotting window hid. This plotting change does not change data, fitting,
likelihoods or source IDs. Point overlap can conceal individual rows visually;
the native arrays retain them all.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/maf_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
